    "lyrics": {
      "text": "The blame-less in the way. Al-le-lu-i--a. Bless-ed art Thou, O Lord, teach me__ Thy sta--tutes. Al--le-lu-i--a.\n\nMy soul hath__ longed to de-sire Thy judg-ments__ at all__ times. Al--le-lu-i--a.\n\nMy soul hath slum-bered from des-pon-den--cy, strength-en me with Thy__ words. Al--le-lu-i--a.\n\nIn-cline my heart un-to thy test-i-mo---nies and not un-to greed-i--ness. Al--le-lu-i--a.\n\nDes-pon-den-cy took hold up-on___ me be-cause of the sin-ners who for-sook Thy__ law. Al--le-lu-i--a.\n\nI_ am a par-tak---er with all them that fear___ Thee, and with them that keep Thy__ com-mand--ments. Al--le-lu-i--a.\n\nGlo-ry to the Fa--ther and to the Son and to the Ho-ly Spir--it. Both now and ev-er and un-to the a-ges of a-ges. A-men. Al-le-lu-i-a.___\n\nThy hands have made me and fash-ioned me; give me un-der-stand--ing and I will learn Thy com--mand---ments. Have mer---cy up-on me, O Lord.\n\nFor I am be-come like a wine-skin in__ frost; yet Thy com-mand-ments have I not for--got---ten. Have mer---cy up-on me, O Lord.\n\nI_ am thine, save me; for af-ter Thy stat-utes__ have I__ sought. Have mer-cy on me, O Lord.\n\nFrom Thy judg-ments I have not de-clined, for Thou has set a__ law for__ me. Have mer-cy on me, O Lord.\n\nI_ have in-clined my heart to per-form thy sta-tutes for ev-er for a__ re-com--pense. Have mer-cy on me, O Lord.\n\nIt is time for the Lord to act; for they have dis--persed Thy__ law. Have mer-cy on me, O Lord.\n\nGlor-y to the Fa-ther and to the Son and to the Ho-ly Spir-it. Both now and ev-er and un-to the a-ges of a-ges. A-men. And have mer-cy on me, O Lord._________\n\nAnd have mer-cy on me. Al--le-lu-i--a. Look up-on me, and have mer--cy on__ me, ac-cord-ing to the judg-ments of those who love Thy name. Al-le-lu-i--a.\n\nI_ am young and ac-count-ed as no-thing, yet Thy sta-tutes have I not for-got-ten. Al-le-lu-i--a.\n\nHear my voice, O__ Lord, ac-cord-ing__ to Thy mer--cy; ac-cord-ing to thy judg-ment, quick-en me. Al-le-lu-i--a.\n\nPrin-ces have per-se-cu-ted me with--out a cause, and be-cause of Thy words my heart hath been a--fraid.__ Al-le-lu-i--a.\n\nMy soul__ shall live and shall praise__ Thee, and Thy judg-ments will help me. I have gone a-stray like a sheep that__ is lost; O Lord seek Thy ser--vant, for I have not for-got-ten Thy com-mand---ments.____"
